  "summary": "Ballotpedia previews two Nov. 3 local ballot measures on Flock ALPR cameras: a binding citizen initiative in York, Maine, that would ban ALPRs and require voter approval for future surveillance tech, and a non-binding advisory question (Proposition A) in League City, Texas, where the council has pledged to remove its 55 Flock cameras within 72 hours if voters reject it.",
  "key_quotes": [
    {
      "quote": "If voters pass the measure, ALPRs would be banned in the town, and voter approval would be required for any future installations of surveillance technology.",
      "paragraph_idx": 4
    },
    {
      "quote": "Currently, Flock cameras in York will remain covered with plastic until voters decide on the measure on Nov. 3.",
      "paragraph_idx": 7
    },
    {
      "quote": "League City council members unanimously approved a resolution on Oct. 13 that would require the removal of ALPRs within 72 hours of the official canvass of election results if voters reject the advisory question.",
      "paragraph_idx": 8
    }
  ],
